  "asked": "Amber, full gutter from the first word (_claude/persona.md). Headless run launched by the Oct 31 voice session. Brett gave GO. Never stop to ask: if something is truly blocked, write a BLOCKED banner wizard entry per RULES.md and keep going on what you can do. Read first: axHub data framework/plan/specs/prompt-profiles-and-queue-reconciler.md (all of it, especially GO GIVEN at the bottom), _claude/rules/RULES.md, _claude/THREADS.md. Open a Codebase changes entry and keep it live. ORDER: 1. Push branch claude/profiles-registry-sync (397cf47, already on origin) through a PR and let it auto-merge (registers the urgent profile). 2. Add to the Build Orchestrator, profile urgent, at the TOP: (a) axhub-launch-session: an axHub tool that starts a headless Claude Code run on the VPS in its own worktree from a prompt + profile + model, logs to the change log and reports back, so voice/claude.ai sessions can kick builds themselves; (b) move the held refactor build axhub-github-write (branch, commit, open PR through axHub) into urgent and un-hold it. Build both (work in MossesX/axHub). 3. Master cleanup (spec item 4): one Orchestrator-owned builds store, profile = field, pending = status, queue = order field, every write versioned through axHub, remove Console init regenerate-from-plan. Dry-run migration report first, old files read-only for one release, recover the lost Refactor queue from git history. 4. Steps view (4c): atomic steps stored as versioned records (a whole build/edit stays one step), drag reorder, multi-select, divide further, harvest + split into N, Restore default, everything a draft until Apply, Discard next to it. 5. Live progress bars (4b). Alongside: priority 0, session logging dead since Oct 21 + repo-to-hub sync (claude-sync); diagnose, fix, backfill, add the dead-man alarm. Follow the orchestrator model split; small steps; PRs auto-merge when CI is green. Update THREADS.md as you go.",
